
For homework 5:

   (1) Edit  hw5.h

       There are 10 machine instructions in this file
       Change the bit patterns to encode the proper machine instruction

       Save the file before running the test

   (2) Test if the instruction codes are correct:

       Type the command in the SSH window:

		run-hw5

       The EDiSim program will simulate the CPU.
       Pick the instruction you want to execute with keys 0,1,2,3

       To execute an instruction:

	   press b once (so Reset = 0)
	   toggle a  4 times to execute 1 instruction

       After executing an instruction, EXAMINING the content of the 
       destination register and verify that the instruction has
       the desired effect.

